Port this Jest test file to Vitest 5. Keep the same behavior.

```js
const { fetchUser } = require('./api')
const { getName } = require('./user')

describe('getName', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    jest.mock('./api', () => ({ ...jest.requireActual('./api'), fetchUser: jest.fn() }))
  })

  test.each([[1, 'Ada'], [2, 'Linus']])('user %i is %s', (id, name, done) => {
    fetchUser.mockResolvedValue({ id, name })
    getName(id).then((result) => {
      expect(result).toBe(name)
      done()
    })
  })
})
```

After upgrading from Vitest 4 to Vitest 5, this test started failing with 'expected spy to be called 1 times, but got 0 times'. Why, and what is the minimal fix?

```ts
import { expect, test, vi, beforeAll } from 'vitest'
import { logger } from './logger'
import { init } from './init'

const spy = vi.spyOn(logger, 'info')

beforeAll(() => {
  init()
})

test('init logs once', () => {
  expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)
})
```
